I was playing around with an interesting phenomenon where you can wish
for a stack of maxint items in wizard mode, then another one, and
#adjust to get a stack of -2147483648 items. This can lead to a number
of interesting things, like wrapping the weight counter so you can
basically carry infinite items (thus letting you create a light source
of radius 13 with a ton of candles), throwing humongous random numbers
of items ("You throw 1120114004 loadstones. Oops... Suddenly, the
dungeon collapses.")

But anyway, my test this time around was putting a stack of such items
into a bag of holding. So I wished for a bag of holding, wished for
2147483647 loadstones, put them in the bag, wished for another one,
put that in the bag, and opened it again to see if they had stacked. I
found that a random wand had been generated inside the bag, along with
my -2147483648 loadstones.

I pulled it out and tested it and...what do you know, it was a wand of
wishing.

At least we answered the question someone had on Freenode's #nethack
the other day, about whether you could get a wand of wishing in a bag
of holding you wished for!


